Basically, no. See https://www.otago.ac.nz/density/pdfs/secr-habitatmasks.pdf for
advice on buffer width. The RB > 0.01 message is a warning based on an approximation, but should not be dismissed lightly.
 Choosing a buffer based on  which estimates you like would be a misuse of statistics. That seems to include your averaging proposal. Use a large buffer unless that extends into non-habitat.

